{"name":"Aqua Sea","hex":"#61a1a9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aqua","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water (as a compound).","A shade of colour, usually a mix of blue and green, most often similar to the colour cyan, though also sometimes closer to turquoise or aquamarine."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a greenish-blue colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aqua"},{"term":"sea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Semai."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large body of salt water.","The ocean; the continuous body of salt water covering a majority of the Earth's surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aqua (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua was a Danish eurodance band, best known for their 1997 single \"Barbie Girl\". The group formed in 1995 in Copenhagen and achieved international success around the world in the late 1990s and early 2000s. The band released three albums: Aquarium in 1997, Aquarius in 2000 and Megalomania in 2011. The group sold an estimated 33 million albums and singles, making them the most profitable Danish band ever."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Aqua_performing_at_Caesars_Windsor%2C_Windsor%2C_Ontario%2C_2025-09-26_30.jpg/330px-Aqua_performing_at_Caesars_Windsor%2C_Windsor%2C_Ontario%2C_2025-09-26_30.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(band)","wikidata":"Q213388"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"},{"title":"Aqua (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua is a variation of the color cyan. The normalized color coordinates for the two web colors named aqua and cyan are identical. It was one of the three secondary colors of the RGB color model used on computer and television displays. In the HSV color wheel aqua is precisely halfway between blue and green. However, aqua is not the same as the primary subtractive color named process cyan used in printing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg/330px-Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(color)","wikidata":"Q372733"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Aqua_Gron_Concert_2008.jpg/500px-Aqua_Gron_Concert_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Aqua_Gron_Concert_2008.jpg/500px-Aqua_Gron_Concert_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aqua at the Grøn Koncert in 2008 (from left: Rasted, Dif, Nystrøm, Norreen)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAqua_Gron_Concert_2008.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Aqua_performing_at_Caesars_Windsor%2C_Windsor%2C_Ontario%2C_2025-09-26_03.jpg/500px-Aqua_performing_at_Caesars_Windsor%2C_Windsor%2C_Ontario%2C_2025-09-26_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Aqua_performing_at_Caesars_Windsor%2C_Windsor%2C_Ontario%2C_2025-09-26_03.jpg/1280px